        "original_id": "22a6b349-942d-5f04-8d82-df92bb9a6467",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Achel Abbey, Cistercians of Strict Observance, monasteries\n- Places: Achel, Campine, Limburg, Flanders, Belgium, Netherlands, Austria, Italy, United States\n- Products: Trappist beer, Authentic Trappist Product\n- Topics: spiritual life, brewery\n\nFacts:\n- Achel Abbey, also called Saint Benedictus-Abbey or Achelse Kluis, belongs to the Cistercians of Strict Observance.\n- Achel Abbey is located in Achel in the Campine region of Limburg, Flanders, Belgium.\n- Achel Abbey is known for its spiritual life and its brewery.\n- Achel Abbey’s brewery is one of the few Trappist beer breweries in the world.\n- Eleven monasteries currently brew beer and sell it as \"Authentic Trappist Product\".\n- Of the eleven monasteries that sell beer as \"Authentic Trappist Product\", six are in Belgium, two are in the Netherlands, and one each is in Austria, Italy, and the United States.",
